 ### [Multi-pass shaded isosurfaces](13612-multi-pass-shaded-isosurfaces.md)
-Multi-pass shaded isosurfaces is a fast approach to display shaded isosurfaces by exploiting rasterization hardware, avoiding the performance loss associated with software-based shading or complex one-pass texture interpolation methods. It sets itself apart from Dachille et al.'s one-pass approach, which relies on 3D texture hardware interpolation combined with software shading and classification, by decomposing the shading computation into multiple rasterization passes.
+Multi-pass shaded isosurfaces is a fast approach to display shaded isosurfaces by exploiting rasterization hardware, avoiding the performance loss associated with software-based shading or complex one-pass texture interpolation methods. It sets itself apart from Dachille et al.'s one-pass approach, which relies on 3D texture hardware interpolation combined with software shading and classification, by decomposing the shading computation into multiple rasterization passes. Choose it when interactive frame rates are required for shaded isosurfaces on standard PC graphics hardware with simple lighting requirements.
 
